meta {
  name: Delete session
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/sessions/:id
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  id: 1
}

docs {
  Deleting a session CASCADES (todo 33): its runs (results), its committee
  signal log and its persisted mock route go with it, plus its boat rows.
  They are keyed by sessionId, so once the session is gone nothing can reach
  them — keeping them only accumulates invisible garbage.

  Expect 200: { status: "deleted", runs: <n>, signals: <n>, routes: <n> } —
  the counts are the entire point of the response: a delete silently taking
  a boat's result with it is the failure mode this covers.

  Expect 404 on a second run of the same id (the session no longer exists).

  Local :3000 shares the LIVE Turso DB — this removes production results,
  with no undo. `node tools/prune-db.js` is the sweep for the orphans that
  predate the cascade.
}
